# %ECSV 1.0
# ---
# datatype:
# - {name: halo_id, datatype: int64}
# - {name: box, datatype: string}
# - {name: enabled, datatype: bool}
# - {name: final_level, datatype: int64}
# - {name: gas, datatype: bool}
# - {name: rvir_min, datatype: float64}
# - {name: queue, datatype: string}
# - {name: nodes, datatype: int64}
# - {name: model, datatype: string}
# - {name: notes, datatype: string}
# meta: !!omap
# - comments: [FOGGIE IC pipeline halo registry -- SEED COPY. This file is not read by the pipeline., '', 'Copy it to your own
#       run tree once, then edit that copy:', '', '    cp $FOGGIE_REPO/initial_conditions/halo_registry.ecsv.example \', '        $FOGGIE_ICS_DIR/halo_registry.ecsv',
#     '', The live registry lives in FOGGIE_ICS_DIR so that each person runs their own, set of halos without colliding
#       in the repo. Nothing here is versioned;, 'if you want your set recorded, commit it somewhere of your own choosing.',
#     '', 'Add a halo by appending one whitespace-separated row below, in the column', order given by the header line.
#       Quote any field containing spaces., 'Then run:  ic_pipeline.py validate-registry', '', enabled              only
#       True rows are ever acted on, 'final_level          top DM level, normally 3', gas                  run a gas stage
#       at the final level, rvir_min             floor on the zoom radius in kpc; 0 uses the box default (80), '', Every
#       row below is enabled = False on purpose. Enabling one commits real, 'resources -- a DM ladder is days of queue time and a gas run is 8-12 TB --',
#     so turn them on deliberately and a few at a time., '', Status is NOT written here -- see status.ecsv in FOGGIE_ICS_DIR.]
